{title: Guide Me, O Thou Great Jehovah}
{artist: William Williams & John Hughes}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[G]Guide me, O thou great Je[C]hovah, [G]pilgrim through this [D]barren land;
[G]I am weak, but thou art [C]mighty — [G]hold me with thy [D]powerful [G]hand.
[C]Bread of [G]heaven, [C]bread of [G]heaven,
feed me till I [D]want no more, feed me till I [D]want no [G]more.

Verse 2
[G]Open now the crystal fountain, [G]Whence the healing [D]stream doth
[G]flow; Let the fire and cloudy [C]pillar [G]Lead me all my [D]journey [G]through.
[C]Strong Deliv'rer, [C]strong Deliv'rer, [G]Be
Thou still my Strength [D]and Shield; Be Thou still my [D]Strength and [G]Shield.

Verse 3
[G]Lord, I trust Thy mighty [G]power, Wondrous are [D]Thy works
[G]of old; Thou deliver'st Thine from [C]thralldom, [G]Who for naught themselves [D]had [G]sold:
[C]Thou didst [C]conquer, Thou [G]didst
conquer, Sin, and Satan [D]and the grave, Sin, and Satan [D]and the [G]grave.

Verse 4
[G]When I tread the verge [G]of Jordan, Bid [D]my anxious
[G]fears subside; Death of deaths, and [C]hell's [G]destruction, Land me safe [D]on [G]Canaan's
[C]side. Songs [G]of [C]praises, songs [G]of
praises, I will ever [D]give to Thee; I will ever [D]give to [G]Thee.

Verse 5
[G]Musing on my habitation, Musing [G]on my heav'nly [D]home, Fills
[G]my soul with holy longings: [C]Come, my [G]Jesus, quickly come; [D]Vanity [G]is
[C]all I [C]see; Lord, [G]I
long to be [D]with Thee! Lord, I long to [D]be with [G]Thee!
